%[text] ## G2 Stage 2 Receiver Integrity
%[text] **Question:** Are the accepted reference and surveillance channels healthy in total in-band power, headroom, DC behavior, and IQ balance?
%[text] **Approach:** run |runG2Stage2ReceiverIntegrity|, which computes whole-channel power via |mean(abs(x).^2)|, uses |pwelch| for PSD review, |bandpower| for low-frequency/DC concentration, and IQ image-risk proxies derived from amplitude, phase, and impropriety metrics.
%[text] **Important:** the current power delta is whole-band baseband power across the captured channel, not isolated direct-path-only energy.
%[text] A negative reference-minus-surveillance value therefore points first to dataset, hardware, or acquisition limitations such as antenna view, gain distribution, or role assignment, not automatically to a broken Stage 2 analysis.
%[text] Clipping, DC, and IQ metrics answer a different question: whether the digitized channels are contaminated or distorted even if the role-based power ordering is poor.
%[text] Figure 2 focuses on whether the accepted reference role actually behaves like a usable reference and whether either channel is operating too close to saturation.
%[text] - Receiver mean power by accepted role uses $ P\_{\\mathrm{mean,dBFS}} = 10\\log\_{10}(\\frac{1}{N}\\sum\_n |x\[n\]|^2 / FS^2) $ for each repetition and each accepted role
%[text] - Reference power advantage uses $ \\Delta P\_{\\mathrm{ref-surv}} = P\_{\\mathrm{ref,dBFS}} - P\_{\\mathrm{surv,dBFS}} $
%[text] - Peak headroom uses $ H\_{\\mathrm{pk}} = 20\\log\_{10}(FS / \\max(|\\Re\\{x\[n\]\\}|,|\\Im\\{x\[n\]\\}|)) $ \
%[text] In the current Stage 2 logic, Figure 2 drives the role-ordering and headroom question: the reference should usually be above surveillance by at least `0 dB`, with `3 dB` shown as the healthier target margin, while very small headroom would raise clipping concern.
%[text] Figure 3 focuses on whether the channels are being invalidated by digitizer or quadrature artifacts instead of only by dataset geometry or gain distribution.
%[text] - Near-rail occupancy uses the fraction of samples where either component is at or above `0.98 * FS`, and exact-rail samples are tracked separately
%[text] - DC spike relative to local PSD floor uses $ D\_{\\mathrm{DC}} = 10\\log\_{10}( PSD(0) / \\mathrm{median}(PSD\_{\\mathrm{local,nonDC}}) ) $
%[text] - I/Q amplitude imbalance proxy uses $ A\_{\\mathrm{IQ}} = 20\\log\_{10}(\\sigma\_I / \\sigma\_Q) $
%[text] - I/Q image-risk proxy uses the impropriety metric $ \\kappa = |E\[x^2\]| / E\[|x|^2\] $ \
%[text] In the current Stage 2 logic, Figure 3 helps decide whether the session should be `reject`, `retune`, or still analytically trusted: severe clipping, severe quantization, or systemic severe DC/IQ behavior can hard-fail receiver integrity, while moderate artifact levels keep the dataset `diagnostic`.
%[text] **Output below:** an interpretation guide, role-mapping table, power-ordering summary, worst receiver metrics, figure guides, the threshold-and-status table, the dual-status interpretation table, the decision traceability table, the per-role channel summary table, and the updated G2 gate row.
if ~exist("datasetId", "var")
    datasetId = "20260622T102123";
    repoRoot = helperResolveRepoRoot();
end

if ~exist("pipelineResults", "var")
    gateIds = localGetGateIds();
    pipelineResults = localInitializePipelineResults(datasetId, repoRoot, ...
        gateIds);
end

if isfield(pipelineResults, "G1Result") && ... %[output:group:07f6a99e]
        pipelineResults.G1Result.Decision == "pass"
    g2Stage2Results = runG2Stage2ReceiverIntegrity(datasetId, repoRoot, ... %[output:606b5ac4] %[output:3347a2c5] %[output:7ae3a09a] %[output:1ffb4470] %[output:0552fdc3]
        struct("ShowFigures", true)); %[output:606b5ac4] %[output:3347a2c5] %[output:7ae3a09a] %[output:1ffb4470] %[output:0552fdc3]
    pipelineResults = localRecordG2Stage2Results(pipelineResults, ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2Summary = localBuildG2Stage2ReviewSummaryTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2AnalysisGuide = localBuildG2Stage2AnalysisGuideTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2RoleMappingSummary = localBuildG2Stage2RoleMappingTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2PowerOrderingSummary = localBuildG2Stage2PowerOrderingTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2WorstMetricsSummary = localBuildG2Stage2WorstMetricsTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2Figure2Guide = localBuildG2Stage2Figure2GuideTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2Figure3Guide = localBuildG2Stage2Figure3GuideTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2ThresholdGuide = localBuildG2Stage2ThresholdGuideTable( ...
        g2Stage2Results);
    g2Stage2InterpretationSummary = ...
        localBuildG2Stage2InterpretationTable(g2Stage2Results);
else
    g2Stage2Results = struct();
    g2Stage2Summary = localBuildBlockedSummaryTable( ...
        "G2 Stage 2 Receiver Integrity", ...
