%[text] ## G3 Sync Analysis Core
%[text] **Question:** does the accepted reference/surveillance mapping support repeatable lag, bounded residual-frequency drift, usable CPI coherence, and one defensible correction strategy across all 15 captures?
%[text] **Approach:** load the baseline session with |IncludeSamples = true|, read |collection\_metadata.json|, and run |helperAnalyzeG3SyncCore|, which uses |finddelay|, |xcorr|, |spectrogram|, and |mscohere| on the frozen G1/G2 contracts.
%[text] **Important:** this section keeps |RF1:RX2| fixed as reference and |RF0:RX2| fixed as surveillance, does not reopen G1 timing or CPI contracts, and reports question-linked manual-review interpretations rather than a final gate verdict.
%[text] Lag evidence focuses on repeatability of the integer lag solution and the peak-to-sidelobe sharpness of the correlation observable.
%[text] Residual-frequency evidence focuses on cross-phase slope over time, phase excursion across each CPI, and whether longer windows remain explainable by one correction model.
%[text] CPI usability focuses on band-mean coherence and pass fraction by |short|, |medium|, and |long| CPI rather than only one session average.
%[text] Strategy comparison focuses on whether |global session|, |per capture|, or |subwindow| correction best explains the short-CPI windows without assuming the most complex option must win.
%[text] **Output below:** a compact G3 review summary, the frozen CPI definitions, the helper question summaries, the strategy comparison summary, the interpretation summary, optional blocking findings, the raw Stage 3 tables, and the updated G3 gate row.
if ~exist("datasetId", "var")
    datasetId = "20260622T102123";
    repoRoot = helperResolveRepoRoot();
end

if ~exist("pipelineResults", "var")
    gateIds = localGetGateIds();
    pipelineResults = localInitializePipelineResults(datasetId, repoRoot, ...
        gateIds);
end

g2GateIdx = localFindGateIndex(pipelineResults, "G2_RF_Health");
g2GateResult = pipelineResults.GateResults(g2GateIdx);

