%   data: {"dataType":"tabular","outputData":{"columnNames":["QuestionId","QuestionText","ChosenObservables","SummaryMetrics","InterpretationLabel","Rationale"],"columns":6,"dataTypes":["string","string","string","string","string","string"],"header":"4×6 table","name":"g4QuestionSummary","rows":4,"type":"table","value":[["\"Q1\"","\"Do the raw\/display axes stay internally consistent and keep the localized direct path near the expected origin neighborhood?\"","\"global-peak origin containment, raw\/display axis centering, direct-path local prominence\"","\"origin_containment=1.000 | median_peak_prominence=9.87 dB\"","\"ready\"","\"Axis plausibility stays tied to the frozen ambgfun coordinate contract and separates origin containment from scene quality.\""],["\"Q2\"","\"Is the stationary scene observable enough that the baseline map is reviewable beyond the direct path alone?\"","\"off-origin nonzero-Doppler energy, off-origin occupied fraction, zero-Doppler ridge fraction, direct-path-to-off-ridge energy\"","\"recommended_cpi=long | median_scene_score=99.76 | median_off_origin_nonzero_doppler=0.998 | median_occupied_minus20dB=0.0000 | median_zero_doppler=0.002 | median_dp_to_off_ridge=40.43 dB\"","\"blocked\"","\"Q2 is scene-first: direct-path contrast is not used to make the scene ready, so a stable leakage\/direct-path product remains blocked or caveated when off-origin nonzero-Doppler evidence is weak.\""],["\"Q3\"","\"Are the baseline maps repeatable across the fixed early, center, and late windows and the 15 repeated captures?\"","\"masked map correlation, direct-path coordinate spread, direct-path width stability\"","\"median_masked_corr=0.891 | max_delay_spread=0.00 samples | max_doppler_spread=0.00 Hz\"","\"ready\"","\"Repeatability focuses on masked linear-power products so the result is not dominated by the direct path or the zero-Doppler ridge.\""],["\"Q4\"","\"Which CPI is provisionally the most defensible downstream baseline under the current descriptive review metrics?\"","\"G3 admissibility, scene observability score, masked repeatability, coordinate stability, shorter-CPI tie-break\"","\"1:long(elig=3.0, scene=99.76, masked=0.966, coord=-0.00) | 2:short(elig=3.0, scene=99.75, masked=0.713, coord=-0.00) | 3:medium(elig=3.0, scene=99.71, masked=0.891, coord=-0.00) | 4:medium_long(elig=2.9, scene=99.75, masked=0.944, coord=-0.00) | 5:short_mid(elig=2.9, scene=99.69, masked=0.837, coord=-0.00)\"","\"blocked\"","\"Q4 ranks scene usefulness before repeatability. A repeatable direct-path-only map cannot rank as ready, and any CPI choice here is G4 due diligence rather than a G6 freeze.\""]]}}
